{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lfun4gf3","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 1 Offline","year":2008,"examDate":2008,"subject":"physics","chapter":"geometrical-optics","chapterGroup":"optics","topic":"refraction-tir-and-prism","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"ptwo-beams-of-red-and-violet-colours-are-made-to-pass-sepa-jee-advanced-physics-motion-fpxpuqsadguc9gn0","content":"<p>Two beams of red and violet colours are made to pass separately through a prism (angle of the prism is 60<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 436.6 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>). In the position of minimum deviation, the angle of refraction will be :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"30<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 436.6 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> for both the colours"},{"identifier":"B","content":"greater for the violet colour"},{"identifier":"C","content":"greater for the red colour"},{"identifier":"D","content":"equal but not 30<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 436.6 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> for both the colours"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lgkjizin/3d46bf0d-50ac-4432-9782-21b053623fef/1e76bdf0-dcf5-11ed-85ee-bd5aa9f0ed3f/file-1lgkjizio.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lgkjizin/3d46bf0d-50ac-4432-9782-21b053623fef/1e76bdf0-dcf5-11ed-85ee-bd5aa9f0ed3f/file-1lgkjizio.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 26 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lgkjizin/3d46bf0d-50ac-4432-9782-21b053623fef/1e76bdf0-dcf5-11ed-85ee-bd5aa9f0ed3f/file-1lgkjizio.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lgkjizin/3d46bf0d-50ac-4432-9782-21b053623fef/1e76bdf0-dcf5-11ed-85ee-bd5aa9f0ed3f/file-1lgkjizio.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lgkjizin/3d46bf0d-50ac-4432-9782-21b053623fef/1e76bdf0-dcf5-11ed-85ee-bd5aa9f0ed3f/file-1lgkjizio.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lgkjizin/3d46bf0d-50ac-4432-9782-21b053623fef/1e76bdf0-dcf5-11ed-85ee-bd5aa9f0ed3f/file-1lgkjizio.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.exa